speechtext:
Yes, for some time they
have been making preparations along those lines. I do not think it is necessary to wait for a report from the tariff board in order to determine a matter of this kind. Then there is another question which has been brought to the attention of the government on several occasions in the last few years, action in regard to which would be of material assistance to the steel industry of Canada;
I refer to a bounty on iron ore. The tariff board have nothing to do with that; they have not been asked to investigate that matter, but it has been looked into by a commission appointed by the Ontario government, a commission composed of competent and experienced men, who have made their report. I am not going into details at the moment; that matter has been placed before the government on several occasions in the past.
